{"title":"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the set of all triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> which have property: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/9/8294983f1b4c6b5465612029691a9aabad838c2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan A,\\tan B,\\tan C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"146\" height=\"16\" /> are positive integers. Prove that all triangles in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> are similar.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If all triangles in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> are similar, then the triplet of angles must be equivalent.\n</p><p><br />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/1/33197052291cf666e6071951235311c2c165a9b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan A = x, \\tan B = y, \\tan C = z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"248\" height=\"16\" />.  Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/2/9924a69668fad613c025da83b041ac85e93243f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B+C = 180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"144\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f3e75cfa9d6445eec9e798810e7aa23f55efd7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = \\tan C = \\tan (180^\\circ - (A+B)) = -\\tan(A+B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nBy applying the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Trigonometric_identities\" title=\"Trigonometric identities\">Angle Addition Identity for Tangent</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/7/707ade4e20b26fb0afbec03ef20ba49572056d55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\tan(A+B) = -\\frac{\\tan A + \\tan B}{1 - \\tan A \\tan B} = \\frac{x+y}{xy - 1} = z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"384\" height=\"41\" />.  Multiplying both sides by the denominator results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a237b831231673e901aa57df043b004bf7cc7e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y = xyz - z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"126\" height=\"14\" />, and rearranging results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/d/09d4ab9648bfd35fda5022a4758577a6b4879b42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z = xyz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"126\" height=\"14\" />.  We want this equation to be satisfied by positive <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integers\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Integers\">integers</a>, and we want to show that there is only one solution permutation.  Thus, we can divide into cases based on the number of ones.\n</p><p><br />\n<b>Case 1: Two variables are 1s</b>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=WLOG\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"WLOG\">WLOG</a>, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbc903b0450aa8b76be5230cc8346b2e23f019a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />.  Substitution results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/3/283b70f38a5218236308b8ea777285142ccfe37a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+z=z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" />, resulting in no solutions.\n</p><p><br />\n<b>Case 2: One variable is 1</b>\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=WLOG\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"WLOG\">WLOG</a>, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. Substitution results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/b/72b70c57359458acbc2c543aa27584f2d21707bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+y+z=yz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"114\" height=\"15\" />, and rearranging the equation results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/c/3bcb381e16b5ff5183741de6a61d37f21f3e0e96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$yz-y-z=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"114\" height=\"15\" />.  By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Simon%27s_Favorite_Factoring_Trick\" title=\"Simon&#39;s Favorite Factoring Trick\">Simon's Favorite Factoring Trick</a>, the equation can be rewritten as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/9/b0919b193fc891561e83ac2515e3bf92380d7d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(y-1)(z-1) = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" />.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/b/a2b0e1404de4eca35c42876bcc83707b753e990e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/6/5e6dc42bb0d892a136cd56c48b13585b42428825.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=2$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> (or vice versa), so a solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/f/dcfc6112a596558ea2b5c4d3009f082ec9763d21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,2,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> in some permutation.\n</p><p><br />\n<b>Case 3: No variables are 1s</b>\n</p><p>Since we already found a solution permutation in Case 2, we want to show that there are no solutions in this case.  We can use <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Induction\" title=\"Induction\">induction</a>.\n</p><p><br />\nFor the base case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/7/3e7ca0304df73768e7c95df0d5712a77bd2e6a31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+2+2 &lt; 2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"149\" height=\"13\" />.  For the inductive step, assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/1/661eff816ac5e733195eca12e538ee09b7eedaec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z &lt; xyz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"126\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=WLOG\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"WLOG\">WLOG</a>, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the variable that is increased.  Adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f79c3676b62fb47243e0d357c87115b6f3395e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" /> to both sides results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/1/731c32fb1f3f22e6d50fb8c7dc9919e937d5151d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy(z+1) &gt; x+y+z + xy$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"214\" height=\"18\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbc903b0450aa8b76be5230cc8346b2e23f019a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/9/ea9ceacfb91f01669ec613eab459d331dcca6aa9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/c/cbcdef0d51fc30abac45a94707417d39fd437e0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z+xy &gt; x+y+z+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"244\" height=\"15\" />.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/b/a8b596689f1e44b038bf79eadb000195e17872fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy(z+1) &gt; x+y+(z+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"220\" height=\"20\" />, so the inductive step is complete.  Therefore, by induction, there are no solutions in this case.\n</p><p><br />\nSince all of the solutions are permutations of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/f/dcfc6112a596558ea2b5c4d3009f082ec9763d21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,2,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a668aa19fac052467c979034e0c8b99a34246c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0^\\circ &lt; A,B,C &lt; 180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"157\" height=\"16\" />, there is only one permutation of angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71bc7a66472f14d58d96e940db6ebc9f101b08e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A,B,C)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" /> where the tangent of each angle results in a permutation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/f/dcfc6112a596558ea2b5c4d3009f082ec9763d21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,2,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />.  Therefore, all of the triangles in set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> are similar.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO\">2006 Indonesia MO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 8\">8</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Indonesia_MO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"Indonesia MO Problems and Solutions\"> All Indonesia MO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017211746\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.043 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 215/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1044/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 52/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6241/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.048      1 Template:Indonesia_MO_box\n100.00%    7.048      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17765:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017211746 and revision id 109975. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}